{
  "an3.68:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 3.68 ",
  "an3.68:0.2": "7. The Great Chapter ",
  "an3.68:0.3": "Followers of Other Religions ",
  "an3.68:1.1": "“Mendicants, if wanderers of other religions were to ask: ",
  "an3.68:1.2": "‘There are these three things. ",
  "an3.68:1.3": "What three? ",
  "an3.68:1.4": "Greed, hate, and delusion. ",
  "an3.68:1.5": "These are the three things. ",
  "an3.68:1.6": "What’s the difference between them?’ ",
  "an3.68:1.7": "How would you answer them?” ",
  "an3.68:1.8": "“Our teachings are rooted in the Buddha. He is our guide and our refuge. Sir, may the Buddha himself please clarify the meaning of this. The mendicants will listen and remember it.” ",
  "an3.68:1.9": "“Well then, mendicants, listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "an3.68:1.10": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "an3.68:1.11": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "an3.68:2.1": "“Mendicants, if wanderers of other religions were to ask: ",
  "an3.68:2.2": "‘There are these three things. ",
  "an3.68:2.3": "What three? ",
  "an3.68:2.4": "Greed, hate, and delusion. ",
  "an3.68:2.5": "These are the three things. ",
  "an3.68:2.6": "What’s the difference between them?’ ",
  "an3.68:2.7": "You should answer them: ",
  "an3.68:2.8": "‘Greed, reverends, is mildly blameworthy, but slow to fade away. Hate is very blameworthy, but quick to fade away. Delusion is very blameworthy, and slow to fade away.’ ",
  "an3.68:3.1": "And if they ask: ‘What is the cause, what is the reason